## `closureSet(x.field)`: whether a closure-typed field holds a closure.
##
## `x.field != nil` written in a module other than the one declaring `field`'s type is emitted as a `(void*)` cast of the closure
## struct, which gcc rejects. The code pointer is the first word of the closure, so this compares that (COMPILER-BUGS.md).

template closureSet*(f: typed): bool =
  cast[ptr pointer](addr f)[] != nil
